abstract: "The Invisible I is an AI Foundations conceptual and behavioral evaluation of the referent a language model assigns to active first-person grammar. The repository defines five non-equivalent written forms—quoted canonical I, quoted reduced i, lowercase index i, active uppercase I, and the unresolved underscore—and provides a fixed eight-prompt protocol for eight planned fresh-instance evaluations across GPT, Claude, Grok, and Gemini in four same-model paired conditions."

